    <summary>Command-line client for OneDev (meta package -&gt; onedev-tod.portable)</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[TOD (TheOneDev) is the official command-line tool for [OneDev](https://onedev.io/), the self-hosted Git server with integrated CI/CD, issue tracking and pull requests. It requires OneDev 16.9.5 or newer.

### Features
- Run CI/CD jobs against uncommitted local changes, branches or tags with live log streaming (`tod build run --local`)
- Check out issues and pull requests into a local working directory (`tod issue checkout`, `tod pr checkout`)
- Query and edit issues, pull requests and builds from the shell
- Inspect build logs, changes and code problem reports
- Check and migrate `.onedev-buildspec.yml` to the latest version (`tod build check-spec`)
- Ships agent skill files so AI coding agents can drive OneDev workflows through `tod`

### Getting started

    tod config set server-url https://onedev.example.com
    tod config set access-token YOUR_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN

The environment variables `ONEDEV_SERVER_URL`, `ONEDEV_ACCESS_TOKEN` and `ONEDEV_TRUST_CERTS_FILE` override the config file.

This is a **meta package**: it installs tod by taking a dependency on [onedev-tod.portable](https://community.chocolatey.org/packages/onedev-tod.portable) and always pulls the matching version.

### Disclaimer
This Chocolatey package is community-maintained and is not created, endorsed, or supported by OneDev Pty.

---

**Note**: This package is automatically updated. If it is out of date by more than a day or two, please contact the maintainer(s).]]></description>
    <dependencies>
